## v0.5.0 (2026-06-08)

- **Zoom the grid from 50% to 200%** using Ctrl/⌘ + scroll wheel, keyboard shortcuts, or the status bar control — filter icons and padding scale to match.
- **Cell formulas are now supported**, and formulas can be copied between cells.
- **Export to SQL** through a new modal that generates INSERT, UPDATE, or UPSERT statements.
- **Automatic over-the-air updates** keep the app current via the Tauri updater.
- Open files faster with the new **⌘O** shortcut — Open File is now the top entry in the command list.
- Close the current sheet with **⌘W**.

- Files opened from the OS (double-click or "Open with") now load correctly on all platforms.
- Fixed an EGL crash on Fedora by stripping bundled libwayland/libEGL from the Linux AppImage.
- Group-by aggregations now coerce numeric text, so xlsx exports total correctly.
- Corrected row rendering and the selection frame while a filter is active.
- The filter header row now keeps its height when reopening the same file.

- Multi-language support (English, Indonesian, Chinese, Spanish) is in progress behind a feature flag and disabled by default in this release.

